  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mahesh Shamlal Nanvani vs The State Of Maharashtra on 9 May, 2019 Author: R. I. Chagla Bench: R. I. Chagla 928-Ba-1292-2019.Doc jsn In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No. 1292 Of 2019 Mahesh Shamlal Nanvani ... Applicant V/s. The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Vinod Sagvikar, i/b. Mr. Umesh Mankapure for the Applicant. Mr. S.R. Agarkar, App for the State. Coram: R. I. Chagla, J. (Vacation Court) Date: 9Th May, 2019 Pc:- 1.",
    "facts": "The Applicant is seeking bail in connection with C.R.No.74/09 registered with Sangli Rural Police Station, under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w 34 of the Indian Penal Code and sections 26(2), 26(2)(iv), 27 r/w 30(2)(A) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 2. The Applicant is arrested on 26/03/2019 and since then he is in custody. He has stated in his FIR that, on 25/03/2019, on prior information, the first informant and others searched a vehicle brought at the premises of Gajanan Transport at Village Budhgaon, Taluka Miraj, District Sangli. On their inspection they found that the truck contained various prohibited articles i.e. Pan Masala worth Rs.5,14,080/- and Tobacco worth Rs.1,52,600/-. The articles were seized. The FIR was lodged. Investigation revealed that the container was driven by one Nawab Shaukatali Taumar. It was dispatched by one Subhash Sharma, who was the owner of Mahalaxi Transport, Delhi and it was to be unloaded at Gajanan Transport at Sangli. After that the goods were to be given to the present Applicant. Based on this FIR, the present Applicant is arrested on 26/03/2019. 3. The FIR is lodged on 25/03/2019 and the Applicant is arrested on 26/03/2019. The Applicant is already in judicial custody. For more than two months he is in custody. The learned APP submits that there are antecedents of similar nature ::: Uploaded on - 11/06/2019 ::: Downloaded on - 12/06/2019 01:09:56 ::: 3/4 56-BA-1292-19 against the Applicant. The investigation is almost over as mentioned by the learned APP. Therefore the Applicant's further Mahesh Shamlal Nanvani vs The State Of Maharashtra on 10 June, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/79514509/ 2 custody is not necessary.",
